---
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes for all component styling; avoid custom CSS unless necessary.
- Follow Shadcn UI component structure and best practices for composability and accessibility.
- Ensure all UI is fully responsive (mobile, tablet, desktop) using Tailwind's responsive utilities.
- Use semantic HTML elements and ARIA attributes for accessibility.
- Prefer functional, stateless components unless local state is required.
- Use Tailwind's dark mode and color system for theme support.
- Avoid inline styles except for dynamic values not supported by Tailwind.

---
description: React & TypeScript Code Quality Rules
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---
- Always use the latest stable versions of React, TypeScript, Next.js, and related libraries.
- Use TypeScript for all new code; avoid using 'any' unless absolutely necessary.
- Prefer explicit types and interfaces for props, state, and function signatures.
- Use React hooks (useState, useEffect, useCallback, etc.) for state and side effects.
- Avoid class components unless required for legacy reasons.
- Use named exports for all components and utilities.
- Write clear, descriptive variable and function names.
- Keep components small and focused; extract logic into hooks or utilities when possible.
- Document complex logic with JSDoc or inline comments.
- Write unit tests for all business logic and critical UI components.

---
description: Next.js App Router & Project Structure
globs: src/app/**/*.{ts,tsx}
---
- Use the Next.js App Router (app directory) for all routing and page structure.
- Organize code by feature (feature folders) rather than by type (e.g., keep related components, hooks, and styles together).
- Use server components for data fetching and static rendering where possible.
- Use client components only for interactive UI.
- Place shared UI components in src/components/ui and feature-specific components in their respective folders.
- Use environment variables for configuration; never hardcode secrets.

---
description: Accessibility & UX Best Practices
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---
- Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible.
- Use semantic HTML and ARIA roles/labels for screen reader support.
- Provide visible focus indicators for all focusable elements.
- Test color contrast and support high-contrast/dark mode.
- Use descriptive alt text for all images and icons.
- Validate forms with clear error messages and accessible feedback.

---
description: General Project Conventions
globs: **/*
---
- Use Prettier for code formatting and ESLint for linting; follow project .prettierrc and .eslintrc configs.
- Commit messages should be clear and follow the Conventional Commits standard.
- Write documentation for all public APIs, utilities, and complex modules.
- Keep dependencies up to date and remove unused packages regularly.
- Review and refactor code for readability and maintainability before merging.

